<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="How Trackwise uses cookies and similar technologies, and how to manage them."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  effective="2026-05-17"
  lastUpdated="2026-05-17"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains what cookies are, which cookies{' '}
    <strong>Trackwise LLC</strong> uses, and how you can manage them.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What is a cookie</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small text file placed on your device by a website. Cookies
    are widely used to make websites work, or work more efficiently, and to
    provide information to site operators.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Categories we use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strictly necessary.</strong> Required for the site to function (session, security, load balancing). Cannot be disabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Preferences.</strong> Language and locale settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> Aggregate, privacy-preserving usage statistics. We do not use third-party advertising cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Specific cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>cf_clearance, __cf_bm</strong> — Cloudflare bot management. Strictly necessary. Session and 30 minutes.</li>
    <li><strong>tw_lang</strong> — Stores selected language. Preferences. 1 year.</li>
    <li><strong>tw_consent</strong> — Stores your cookie-banner choice. Strictly necessary. 6 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Most browsers allow you to refuse or delete cookies. Refer to your
    browser's documentation. Disabling strictly necessary cookies may break
    parts of the site.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    We honor the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal where required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:privacy@trackwise.finance">privacy@trackwise.finance</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
